We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
h(\blueD{1})&=\dfrac{(\blueD{1})^2-8(\blueD{1})+7}{(\blueD{1})^2-2(\blueD{1})+1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1-8+7}{1-2+1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac00
\end{align}$

We got the **indeterminate form** $\dfrac00$ (step D).

Now we need to determine which analytical method is applicable.

Since we have a quotient with polynomial expressions, we will use the method of **factoring** (step E):

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{x^2-8x+7}{x^2-2x+1}&=\dfrac{\cancel{(x-1)}(x-7)}{\cancel{(x-1)}(x-1)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x-7}{x-1}
\end{align}$

Now we can try **direct substitution** (step A) once again!

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{(\blueD{1})-7}{(\blueD{1})-1}&=\dfrac{-6}{0}
\end{align}$

We got $\dfrac{b}{0}$ where $b\neq0$.

This means that $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 1}h(x)$ doesn't exist because there is a vertical **asymptote** at that $x$-value (step B).
